WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.730
I don't think we're going to get this attic 
cleaned up by the end of the year.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.000
Yuzu, could you take that 
box of clothes outside?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:10.850
Okay.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.440
Okami-san, what should I do 
about the stuff in here?

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.240
We haven't used those in centuries.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.070
Just throw them all out.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.080
I wonder what this is.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.100
A scroll?

00:01:51.290 --> 00:02:01.010
<b>Konohana Kitan</b>

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Epsiode 12:   
Miracle on New Year's Eve</b>

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:10.180
Did you make this for us, Ren-chan?

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.430
All the chefs have gone 
home for the holidays.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.260
You're so good at cooking, Ren-chan.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.530
I bet you'll make a spectacular wife.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.200
Oh, cut it out.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.780
I just boiled some soba 
that I bought at the store.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.910
Don't you have to visit home, Natsume?

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.290
My nephews would just nag and 
pester me for New Year's money.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:29.260
<i>That's</i> why you aren't?

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:32.830
Though I wouldn't mind.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.410
The snow has let up.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.820
Should we go this year?

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:35.790
Yay!

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.060
That sounds fun.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.280
Especially since we have Yuzu this year.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.880
To the shrine for New Year's.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.510
I can't believe you don't even 
have a haori, Yuzu-chan.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.470
Here, hurry up.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.150
I'll lend you my—

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.820
Are you okay?

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.740
Jeez, what is this?

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.490
Sorry, I was cleaning Okami-san's 
room, and I found it there.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:00.240
Let's get going.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.350
Hey, isn't that a kenzoku scroll?

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:05.400
Kenzoku?

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.950
Those are people who work at shrines, right?

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:13.050
Okami-san said I could throw it out, 
but I'm so curious about it.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.900
It looks really old.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.930
And why was it in Okami's room?

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:17.960
That's perfect.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.410
Let's take it to the shrine with us.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.120
We might learn about Okami's secret past.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.260
Okami-san's past?

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.260
I'm in.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.710
The scarier it is, 
the more interesting, huh?

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.480
It's so cold.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.580
The shrines in the city are open this late?

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.520
That's a cute hood, Yuzu.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.170
I'm going to go draw a fortune.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:42.740
Right?

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:44.400
Hey, dummy!

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.360
We need to go do our prayers first.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.940
What should I pray for?

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:50.720
We have another dummy here.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:51.570
What's your problem?

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:58.310
Listen, we're here to thank the gods 
that we got through the year well.

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:02.810
Only a human would visit a shrine for the 
first time in ages just to ask for more wishes.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:04.750
Really?

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:09.150
I've never seen so many 
people so late in the day.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.170
I want to get in the kotatsu.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.160
I hate the cold.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.650
Y-You're right.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.290
Okay, next.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.740
It's our turn.

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.610
I want to ring the bell!

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.860
Be quiet when you're in 
the presence of the gods.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.280
All right, make a line.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.990
<i>This time last year,</i>

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:33.860
<i>I would have never dreamed 
that my life would be so lively.</i>

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:45.330
<i>God, thank you for bringing 
me to all of my new friends.</i>

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.000
The New Year's Eve bells are starting.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.860
Aren't they doing them here?

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:54.590
The New Year's Eve bells are at the temple.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.330
We're at the shrine.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:59.820
I brought this with me, but who should I ask?

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.080
Wait!

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.950
Huh? Where am I?

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.790
Is anyone there?

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:28.400
So busy...

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.520
So busy...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.210
Where did I put it?

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.580
It's almost the end of the year...

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:34.580
I don't have time!

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.730
Man, there's so much to do.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.770
U-Um, excuse me...

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.950
Can someone tell me where I am?

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.730
Don't just stand there 
in the middle of the road.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.360
I'm busy, you know.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.110
S-Sorry!

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.690
Oh, we're in the same business.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.150
Come with me, then.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:59.680
U-Um...

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.730
Welcome back, Tsubaki.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.550
You're late, Tsubaki.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.270
Sorry, I picked up one of 
our people along the way.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.060
Can you carry these, then?

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:28.710
Huh?

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:34.530
<i>They're the same as the scroll 
that was at Konohanatei.</i>

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.900
Hachibei from Nichome again?

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:40.060
"I wish my wife would come back to me"?

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.000
It's because you drink all the 
time instead of doing your job!

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.950
How am I supposed to answer such a prayer?

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:47.990
And turn down all the prayers of people 
who haven't made their offerings.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:51.010
Ignore everyone who doesn't follow the 
two bow, two clap, one bow routine.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.020
You're too strict, Senpai.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.490
Um...

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:57.590
Please make Ma's coughing stop.

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.680
Please, God.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.980
The good cough medicine 
is on the third shelf.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:08.030
He hasn't made his offering, though.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.890
He hasn't clapped, though.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:11.000
Shut up!

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.180
We're back.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:17.050
We fixed the dried-up well in Icchome.

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:17.840
Good job.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:26.460
Is your job here to grant people's wishes?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.460
You came here not even knowing that?

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:31.070
That's amazing!

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:32.870
What a noble profession!

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.200
I guess.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.950
It kind of is that big of a deal.

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:39.300
We don't grant just anyone's wishes.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:43.850
It depends on whether we, the kenzoku, 
feel like they deserve our help,

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:47.360
and whether they're wishing this 
for someone other than themselves.

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:52.090
People can't make wishes for themselves?

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.010
Of course not.

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:56.700
Those wishes are for people 
to grant themselves.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.660
The human world is built on 
people helping each other.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.590
Our job as gods is just 
to help them do that.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:08.580
Th-That's such a gracious mission!

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:09.730
I'm so moved!

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.500
What is this funny creature?

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:15.570
Well, she had a scroll, and I thought she 
was one of ours, so I brought her here.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.340
Oh, right!

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:21.190
I came here to ask about this scroll.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:25.250
This has someone else's seal on it.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.560
It can only be opened by that person.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.810
Who does it belong to?

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.180
Well...

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:35.850
I've got the gist of the situation.

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:40.860
You found that scroll at an inn called 
Konohanatei, where you work.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:41.620
Yes.

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:45.340
What do you think, Tsubaki?

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:47.380
It doesn't look like she's lying, does it?

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.180
The scroll is real, too.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:54.000
Which means I brought her here by accident.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.450
So...

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.720
What's your name?

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.210
My name is Yuzu.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:08:59.870
Okay, Yuzu.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.430
I hate to say this, but...

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:08.350
Konohanatei doesn't exist in this world.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.110
Huh?

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:15.620
I'm saying that you can't go back home.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.570
Yuzu!

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:29.280
Hey, have you seen Yuzu?

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:31.610
Well, it's so crowded.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:35.120
I told her to go back to 
Konohanatei if she gets lost.

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:37.040
She's not a child.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.770
I know, but...

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.320
I have a really bad feeling about this.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.570
Wh-What do you mean, I can't go home?

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.640
Kozue!

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:48.760
Are you all right?

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.890
I'm sorry, Tsukushi.

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:53.310
And at the busiest time of the year...

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.120
It's fine.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:56.490
You've been working non-stop.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:10:01.050
But if I collapse, we won't 
have enough record keepers.

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:02.270
Um...

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:05.340
I can read and write.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:07.580
If there's anything I can help with...

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.200
Sit here.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.420
Here, sumi ink and a brush.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:13.870
Write the visitors' names and wishes here.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:15.620
They're gonna come one after another. Quickly!

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:16.750
O-Okay.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.230
Once he's gone, I can get promoted.

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:22.920
Punish that woman for 
taking my husband away.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:24.320
<i>I hear people's wishes in my head.</i>

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:24.130
I want money.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:26.930
<i>Their malice, and what's 
really in their hearts...</i>

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:31.110
Thank you for curing my mother's sickness.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:35.200
My daughter-in-law had a healthy boy.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:38.950
I found a new job thanks to the gods.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.830
Thank you.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.700
Thank you.

00:10:44.020 --> 00:10:45.610
We're done!

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:48.090
Now we can rest until morning.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.330
Get some rest while you can.

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:53.670
I'm so sorry.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:56.020
This is all because I collapsed.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:57.560
It's all right.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.360
Are you okay now?

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.580
Yes, thank you.

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:04.880
You all have such a tough job.

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:08.800
It's hard, but the people who 
make wishes at the shrine

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:11.360
are all people who had nowhere else to turn.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:12.620
We can't just leave them.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:17.640
But where did you learn to read and write?

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:20.920
I learned from Yaobikuni-sama.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:23.570
Yaobikuni, you say?

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:27.200
I know that priestess well.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.410
G-Goddess...

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.840
What does she mean by goddess?

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.340
Inari Ohkami.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.380
She's the goddess of Ukanomitama.

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:44.230
Well, well. Are you the
aforementioned priestess's kenzoku?

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:45.000
Oh...

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.710
I'm not a kenzoku, but rather
an attendant at an inn.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.220
An attendant?

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:52.950
I see.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.670
She was lost in the path of the gods,

00:11:56.670 --> 00:12:00.430
when you, Tsubaki, 
brought her here by accident.

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:01.270
Yes.

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:05.770
Um... What is this "path of the gods"?

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:08.460
You know how there are 
Inari shrines all over the place?

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.980
The gods can be at all the shrines because

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.990
we use the path of the gods to get around.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:16.560
The path takes us not just 
to different locations,

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:17.950
but to different times, as well.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:25.800
In other words, in this world, or rather, 
this age, Konohanatei doesn't exist.

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:29.550
I've never heard of a 
hot spring for the gods.

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:30.620
A hot spring?

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:34.550
I know! Let's dig up a hot spring.

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:37.320
Don't say that like we're 
going to dig up potatoes!

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:40.400
There are too many Inari shrines these days.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.180
I can't manage all of them.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:45.270
I want to dig up a hot spring and relax a bit.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:46.840
I have spending money, too.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:49.000
Please don't be so blunt.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:52.540
U-Um, so what should I do?

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.130
What else?

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.290
It was fate that brought you here.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.730
You should just stay here.

00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:01.170
<i>I figured she'd say that.</i>

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:07.520
Goddess, could we at least keep 
her here as one of the kenzoku?

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:10.810
She's educated, and she learns quickly.

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:12.980
I'm sure she'll be useful.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.850
Yeah, you should work here, Yuzu.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.270
Sounds good!

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:21.050
It's an honorable thing, 
to be able to work for the gods.

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:23.380
B-But...

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:26.240
You don't need to do 
maid work for a travel lodge.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:26.940
But...

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:32.720
I-I want to go home to Konohanatei!

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:37.340
I-I'm sorry!

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:39.690
You don't need to apologize.

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:42.100
Sorry for calling it maid work.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:45.040
You must have an important job there.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.780
No, I've been working there 
for less than a year.

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:49.290
I'm the lowest worker there.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.190
Um...

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.530
Then who's going to care 
if you're not there?!

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.350
Why are you so desperate to go back?

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:00.100
You're absolutely right.

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:02.670
Uh, sorry. I was in the wrong.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:03.310
Sorry.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:09.490
S-Still, Konohanatei is the 
only place I can go home to.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.940
They're all my precious friends.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:18.670
So then, Yuzu, say you 
get home to Konohanatei.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.300
How long can you be 
there with your friends?

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:26.130
You're all going to go your 
own ways eventually, right?

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:30.000
Once I'm free to resign, I'm going 
to aim to become a priestess again.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.650
You're going to end up separated eventually.

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:36.760
So do you insist on going home?

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:40.850
Well...

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:44.200
Because I've already met them.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:49.170
I can't go back to being 
who I was before I met them.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:53.800
He'd never have talked to me 
like that if I served an Inari shrine.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:59.580
Even if we're going to part 
ways someday, even then,

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:03.880
I can't help but love all the 
friends I've met at Konohanatei,

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.800
and all those people, too.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:14.500
You're such an idiot.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:19.560
Haven't you thought that maybe you could 
go home if you'd written in a scroll

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.900
that you want to go home 
for the sake of someone else?

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.580
I never thought of that!

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:29.940
But I'm so useless, I wouldn't be 
useful to anyone if I went back.

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:34.730
Although that's not a wish that 
simple kenzoku like us could grant.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:36.860
I'm sure it'll work out.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:38.000
Don't overthink it.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:42.120
We might not be able to take 
her back with our powers,

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.840
but there might be someone 
who'll hear her wish.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:50.130
<b>Hot Springs Galore</b>

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:47.600
Sure, do what you can.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:50.120
So you aren't going to help us, are you?

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:53.650
Do any of you have connections 
with a powerful kenzoku?

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:55.840
Th-Thank you.

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:59.540
Tsubaki's a newcomer here, like you.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:04.310
The shrine where she worked 
was washed away by a landslide.

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:08.580
She's been a kenzoku all her life, moving 
from shrine to shrine since she was little.

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:13.840
So she doesn't have a home 
to return to like you do.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:16.390
Whoops, I said too much.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:17.950
She's going to yell at me again.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.910
No luck, huh?

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:36.440
You'd have to be hundreds 
of years old to time travel.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:41.560
Where are we going to find 
such a powerful fox?

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:42.350
<b>Konohanatei</b>

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:49.630
Why are those kids out so late?

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:00.990
Yuzu, that scroll...

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.490
Come home.

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:17.510
Look at that.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:22.760
There's someone over there who's 
wishing for you to come home.

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:30.810
Get going.

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:46.520
Next year!

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:48.460
Hey, want to write something?

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.130
O-Okay.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.260
You'll gain weight if 
you eat so late at night.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.970
How is a doll going to gain weight?

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.740
That idiot... Where is she?

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:05.750
It's almost New Year's.

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:09.050
107...

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.290
Hurry up and get back here.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.830
Happy New Year!

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:31.050
Why do you always show up out of the blue?

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.120
Satsuki-chan!

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:33.890
Satsuki-chan!

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:35.400
Satsuki-chan!

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:38.860
I thought I'd never see you again!

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:43.880
Why are you making such 
a big deal about getting lost?

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:47.380
You can't wander off like that.

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:48.530
Okay.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:50.820
Okay. I'm sorry.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.060
Sorry for worrying you.

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:57.780
Okay, let's try that again.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:05.540
Happy New Year!

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:10.380
Let's give Konohanatei 
all we've got this year.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:16.710
You're late.

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:19.490
Sorry. You were asleep, so...

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.590
Sorry for making you worry.

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:24.530
I wasn't worried.

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:27.570
Happy New Year, Okami-san!

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:28.590
Sure, sure.

00:19:28.590 --> 00:19:29.430
Happy New Year.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.150
Yuzu.

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:33.910
Where did you get that hood?

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:37.020
Oh, Ren-chan lent it to me.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.230
Yeah?

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:39.640
Okay, fine.

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:41.880
We have work tomorrow.

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:43.410
Don't sleep in.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.070
H-Hey, Okami-san...

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:50.030
I'm home.

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:54.120
Yeah.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:55.600
Welcome home.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:17.020
A hot spring is going to need good food.

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:19.350
Are you talking about 
relaxation therapy again?

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:22.370
It's just going to go bust.

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:25.560
Then we'll just lend it out to other gods.

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:28.520
Why don't we make it a hot spring inn?

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:30.380
Here we go again with your nonsense.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:31.830
It would be fun.

00:20:32.050 --> 00:20:35.010
You'll have to help when we do, Tsubaki.

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:35.990
Whatever.

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.540
A hot spring inn?

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:41.420
<i>I'm an attendant at an inn.</i>

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:44.640
<i>It's a hot spring inn for the gods.</i>

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:47.410
It couldn't be.

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:56.310
<b>I wish for a warm home for Tsubaki-san. 
- Yuzu</b>

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.310
That clumsy meddler of a fox...

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:58.140
It was Yanagi, wasn't it?

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.820
She just had to go and do that.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:06.850
I wish for the person written here

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:11.150
to return to the people who await 
her when she becomes lost.

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:12.570
Tsubaki.

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:18.170
I bet she'll get lost again.

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:26.130
<i>Where I wandered into</i>

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:31.480
It was such a long time ago, 
I'd totally forgotten about it.

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:32.690
<i>was a beautiful place</i>

00:21:32.340 --> 00:21:36.540
I don't remember the name or the face 
of that fox girl I met that night.

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:37.110
<i>But there are people waiting for me</i>

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:40.240
I think she was wearing a red hood.

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:44.480
<i>So I will be returning home</i>

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:44.790
Okami-san, I'm home.

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:53.770
<i>From the snowy night sky, I hear them calling</i>

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:52.740
Yeah.

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:54.360
Welcome home.

00:21:54.180 --> 00:22:04.950
<i>They're here so clearly in my heart</i>

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:15.140
<i>I can't return to yesterday</i>

00:22:15.780 --> 00:22:26.580
<i>The many "thank yous" in my dreams</i>

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:37.060
<i>I hope they reach the people I love</i>

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:44.200
<i>Until we meet again</i>

00:22:54.270 --> 00:22:58.220
"I wish for a warm home for Tsubaki-san."

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:05.860
<b>Konohanatei</b>

00:23:06.860 --> 00:23:08.330
It's so cold!

00:23:08.330 --> 00:23:11.400
The guests should be coming any minute.

00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:13.190
Hurry up, Nacchan.

00:23:13.190 --> 00:23:13.990
Okay.

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:16.360
Yuzu, go ahead and greet them.

00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:17.980
Okay, got it.

00:23:17.980 --> 00:23:18.660
Thanks.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:30.600
Welcome, guest.

00:23:31.110 --> 00:23:33.570
Welcome to Konohanatei.

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Thank you for watching!</b>

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:37.350
Merlion!
